    a <ontology/EvidenceQuote/#resource> ;
    rdfs:label "Evidence for Gum Lac, Seed, Shell, Stick, and Dye used in Varnish, Paint & Lacquer: Mortimer (1823), General Commercial Dictionary, scan p. 508"@en ;
    <ontology/quoteText/#resource> "When the spirit of wine is very strong, it will dissolve a greater proportion of the seed-lac; but this quantity will saturate the common, which is seldom of a strength sufficient to make varnishes in perfection. 498"@en ;
